WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.760
How old is SCP-106 really? Is this ferocious&nbsp;
fogie really as ancient as you think?

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.920
Depends on who you think he is.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.560
If you think he’s actually Dr. Robert&nbsp;
Scranton, who disappeared into SCP-3001&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.360
as an adult back in the year 2000, he’s&nbsp;
likely between 60 and 80 years old.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.560
If you believe he’s actually Corporal&nbsp;
Lawrence, who was an adult likely in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.960
his thirties during World War One, he’d&nbsp;
currently be well over a century old.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.480
And if you’re really spicy, and believe he’s a&nbsp;
holdover from a whole species of SCP-106s who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.720
went into hibernation when his species went&nbsp;
extinct, he’s likely been alive for anywhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:41.440
between 40,000 to 130,000 years. Now that’s a&nbsp;
whole lot of birthday candles to try and blow out!&nbsp;

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.440
No wishes granted for this guy this year.
My god, he really is an Old Man...

